w 6: all empty\n\nRow 5: d5 has NWF1 (White Knight)\n\nSo e7 is empty. So moving N from d5 to e7 would be possible, and that would check the Black king on c8.\n\nIs that correct? Let's verify the knight move from d5 to e7. Yes, d5 to e7 is a knight's L-shape (1 right, 2 up). Then, from e7, the knight attacks c8 (since e7 to c8 is 2 left, 1 up, which is another L-shape). So yes, that's a check.\n\nSo Nxe7+ is a check. Now, what can Black do in response? The Black king is on c8. Possible escapes:\n\n- Move to b8, b7, c7, d7, d8.\n\nBut knight on e7 is checking, so king must move out of check.\n\nPossible squares:\n\nb8: is it attacked? The knight on e7 attacks d5, c6, etc., but not b8. Wait, from e7, knight moves to c8 (check), but what squares does it attack around c8?\n\nWait, the check is from e7 to c8. So the king must move to a square not attacked by the knight. The knight on e7 attacks:\n\nc8 (current king position), and other squares like d5, f5, g6, g8, f9 (invalid), etc. Wait, from e7, knight's moves are:\n\nc6 (left 2, down 1), d5 (left 1, down 2), f5 (right 1, down 2), g6 (right 2, down 1), g8 (right 2, up 1), f9 (invalid), d9 (invalid), c8 (left 2, up 1). Wait, c8 is two left and one up from e7 (e to c is two left, 7 to 8 is one up). Yes, so knight on e7 attacks c8.\n\nSo when the knight moves to e7, it checks the king on c8.\n\nBlack king's possible moves:\n\nb8: is it under attack? The knight on e7 doesn't attack b8. Let's see: from e7 to b8 is three left and one up, which isn't a knight move. So b8 is safe.\n\nb7: e7 to b7 is three left, which isn't a knight move. So b7 is safe.\n\nc7: adjacent, but is it attacked? The knight on e7 doesn't attack c7. c7 is two left and zero up/down from e7? No. So c7 is safe.\n\nd7: from e7 to d7 is one left, which is not a knight move. So d7 is safe.\n\nd8: e7 to d8 is one left and one up, not a knight move. Safe.\n\nSo Black king can move to b8, b7, c7, d7, d8.\n\nBut are any of those squares attacked by other White p